      "comment": "The choice value is scaled by the source's FRESHNESS: with equal urgency and cost, a shopper prefers the fresher stall (a stale source ranks lower). Fresh (1.0) is unchanged. The freshness weighting is CONSULTED FROM HELD KNOWLEDGE: only a shopper who HOLDS a DegradationLaw (holds_law) weighs a stall's freshness; a naive shopper does not. The decision reads held knowledge, it is not imposed by the engine. And an APPETITE dimension (automatic, from satiety): a stall selling the food the shopper is sick of (src.good == their last_food) is weighed down by their satiety (1 - satiety) -- 'what do I feel like'. The choice is one COLLAPSE over all held dimensions (urge x preference x freshness-belief x appetite); adding a dimension does not touch the Argmax. (Body layer: the appetite dimension is read from the BODY -- has_body -- the mind reading its body's satiety.)"
